        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/mass_effect_brighter.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p><em>Oof. </em>I expected this day to come but the news has left me winded nonetheless; BioWare, the creator of so many beloved role-playing series and games - <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/mass-effect\">Mass Effect</a>, Dragon Age, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/baldurs-gate\">Baldur's Gate</a>, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/star-wars-knights-of-the-old-republic\">Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic</a> - has been closed. <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/bioware-closing-down-mass-effect-5-cancelled\">EA decided it had no place for it under its new Saudi and private investment ownership</a>. So <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/mass-effect-5\">Mass Effect 5</a> has been canned, and a studio that helped shape an industry and popularise role-playing games over the course of 31 years is no more.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/far",
